      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to calculate the total number of rounds played and divide it by the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see that:\n- 5 golfers played 1 round.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds.\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds.\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 1 \\text{ round/golfer} = 5 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 2 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 4 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 3 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 6 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 3 \\text{ golfers} \\times 4 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 12 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\\[ 5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 5 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 25 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total number of rounds played:\n\\[ 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 56 \\text{ rounds} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ golfers} + 2 \\text{ golfers} + 2 \\text{ golfers} + 3 \\text{ golfers} + 5 \\text{ golfers} = 17 \\text{ golfers} \\]\n\nThe average number of rounds played by each golfer is the total number of rounds divided by the total number of golfers:\n\\[ \\frac{56 \\text{ rounds}}{17 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 3.3 \\]\n\nRounding 3.3 to the nearest whole number gives:\n\\[ \\boxed{3} \\]",
