      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to calculate the total number of rounds played and then divide by the total number of golfers.\n\nFirst, let's list the number of rounds played by each golfer:\n- 1 round: 5 golfers\n- 2 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 3 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 4 rounds: 3 golfers\n- 5 rounds: 5 golfers\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 1 \\text{ round each} = 5 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 2 \\text{ rounds each} = 4 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 3 \\text{ rounds each} = 6 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\text{ golfers} \\times 4 \\text{ rounds each} = 12 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 5 \\text{ rounds each} = 25 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total number of rounds:\n\\[\n5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 52 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\nThe average number of rounds played by each golfer is the total number of rounds divided by the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n\\frac{52 \\text{ rounds}}{17 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 3.0588\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
