      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we start by calculating the total number of round played by every golfer. According to the given chart, we have the number of golfers who played each number of rounds:\n\n- 1 round: 5 golfers\n- 2 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 3 rounds: 2 golfers\n- 4 rounds: 3 golfers\n- 5 rounds: 5 golfers\n\nThe total number of rounds played can be computed as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Total rounds} = (1 \\text{ round} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers}) + (2 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers}) + (3 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers}) + (4 \\text{ rounds} \\times 3 \\text{ golfers}) + (5 \\text{ rounds} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers})\n\\]\n\\[\n= 5 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25\n\\]\n\\[\n= 52\n\\]\n\nNext, we determine the total number of golfers by summing up all golfers across all rounds:\n\\[\n\\text{Total golfers} = 5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 17\n\\]\n\nThen, we calculate the average number of rounds played per golfer:\n\\[\n\\text{Average number of rounds} = \\frac{\\text{Total rounds}}{\\text{Total golfers}} = \\frac{52}{17}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we compute the average and round to the nearest whole number:\n\\[\n\\frac{52}{17} \\approx 3.0588\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.0588 to the nearest whole number gives \\( 3 \\).\n\nThus, the average number of rounds played by each golfer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
