      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to calculate the total number of rounds played and then divide by the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see that:\n- 5 golfers played 1 round\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of rounds played:\n- The 5 golfers who played 1 round contributed \\(5 \\times 1 = 5\\) rounds.\n- The 2 golfers who played 2 rounds contributed \\(2 \\times 2 = 4\\) rounds.\n- The 2 golfers who played 3 rounds contributed \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) rounds.\n- The 3 golfers who played 4 rounds contributed \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) rounds.\n- The 5 golfers who played 5 rounds contributed \\(5 \\times 5 = 25\\) rounds.\n\nAdding these together, the total number of rounds played is:\n\\[5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 52\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the total number of golfers. From the chart, we can see that there are:\n\\[5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17\\] golfers.\n\nNow, we can calculate the average number of rounds played by each golfer:\n\\[\n\\text{Average number of rounds} = \\frac{\\text{Total number of rounds}}{\\text{Total number of golfers}} = \\frac{52}{17} \\approx 3.0588\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.0588 to the nearest whole number, we get:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
